From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: St0neWan9 <pawamaba@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:50:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: bridge: re-arm the autofill accept guard when the
 shell's dropdown gets new rows

Plan B148. AutofillPopupControllerImpl ignores a choice until its
accidental-click guard (barrier_for_accepting_) has run, and Show() resets
the guard whenever the dropdown is shown again for new rows (a two-step
sign-in's password field, passkeys that arrive after the passwords).
Chrome re-arms it from PopupViewViews::OnPaint(); the shell's dropdown has
no Views paint, and ShellAutofillPopupView called OnPopupPainted() only
from Show(). So after any row update every choice was ignored: the form
was filled by the preview at most, and the dropdown stayed open over the
page, taking clicks meant for the page.

OnSuggestionsChanged() now re-arms the guard after publishing the new
rows, as a repaint would.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 openarc/bridge/oac_autofill.mm | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/openarc/bridge/oac_autofill.mm b/openarc/bridge/oac_autofill.mm
index d0086fe9059e..c29e02b3300c 100644
--- a/openarc/bridge/oac_autofill.mm
+++ b/openarc/bridge/oac_autofill.mm
@@ -615,6 +615,13 @@ void OnSuggestionsChanged(bool prefer_prev_arrow_side) override {
       selected_ = -1;
     }
     Publish(/*notify=*/true);
+    // Plan B148: new rows for a dropdown that is already showing (Chrome
+    // reuses the view, for example when a sign-in page's passkeys arrive after
+    // its passwords) reset the controller's accidental-click guard, and Chrome
+    // re-arms it when its view paints the new rows. The shell redraws them, so
+    // re-arm it here as Show() does; otherwise every later choice was ignored
+    // and the dropdown stayed open.
+    controller_->OnPopupPainted();
   }
 
   bool OverlapsWithPictureInPictureWindow() const override { return false; }
